def text_w(s, size, style="normal"):
    prop = FontProperties(family="DejaVu Serif", style=style)
    return 1.06 * max(TextPath((0, 0), line, size=size, prop=prop).get_extents().width
                      for line in s.split("\n")) / 72


def walk(n, d=0):
    n["d"] = d
    yield n
    for _, kids in n["branches"]:
        for k in kids:
            yield from walk(k, d + 1)


def layout(root):
    nodes = list(walk(root))
    depth = max(n["d"] for n in nodes) + 1
    colw = [max(max(text_w(n["name"], FS_NAME), text_w(n["venue"], FS_VENUE, "italic")) + 2 * PAD
                for n in nodes if n["d"] == d) for d in range(depth)]
    gapw = [max([text_w(p, FS_PROB, "italic") for n in nodes if n["d"] == d for p, _ in n["branches"]], default=0)
            + TRUNK + 2 * LABEL_PAD + BUS for d in range(depth - 1)]
    xs = [MARGIN]
    for d in range(depth - 1):
        xs.append(xs[-1] + colw[d] + gapw[d])
    for n in nodes:
        n["x"], n["w"] = xs[n["d"]], colw[n["d"]]
    return xs[-1] + colw[-1] + MARGIN


def place(n, cur):
    """Leaves take consecutive rows; a parent sits midway between its first and last junction."""
    if not n["branches"]:
        n["y"] = cur[0]
        cur[0] += PITCH
        return n["y"]
    n["stems"] = []
    for _, kids in n["branches"]:
        ys = [place(k, cur) for k in kids]
        n["stems"].append((ys[0] + ys[-1]) / 2)

input.prompt:
Today is October 2026. I'm checking novelty of a speculative-decoding idea before building it. The idea: parallel / block-diffusion drafters (DFlash, arXiv 2602.06036, ICML 2026; PARD 2504.18583; ParallelSpec 2410.05589; P-EAGLE 2602.01469; DSpark 2607.05147; SpecDiff 2408.05636) produce a probability distribution for every draft position in ONE drafter forward pass. Instead of verifying only the top-1 chain (what DFlash does), build a token TREE from those per-position distributions (e.g. top-k branching at low-confidence positions, chosen under a fixed verification budget of N tree nodes, Sequoia/EAGLE-2-style), and verify it losslessly with tree attention in one target pass. Since the drafter cost does not grow with tree width/depth, the tree is "free" on the draft side; the budget N would also adapt to serving load (verification gets compute-bound at high batch).

Search arXiv / Google Scholar / OpenReview / GitHub (DFlash repo z-lab/dflash or similar, vLLM, SGLang, speculators) thoroughly for prior or concurrent work that does any of:
1. token-tree (or multi-draft / lattice) verification built from a parallel or diffusion drafter's per-position marginals (e.g. DiffuSpec "causal-consistency path search", DFlash tree mode, PARD with trees, Gumiho, Falcon, "lattice", "beam over block diffusion draft", "TreeDiff", "Spiffy" etc.);
2. budget/cost-model-driven tree sizing that adapts to batch size / load (e.g. Sequoia hardware-aware, EAGLE-2 dynamic, SmartSpec/TurboSpec/AdaSpec, "batch-aware tree", "BASS", "ProPD", "Dynamic tree for serving");
3. fixing the independence problem of parallel drafts (position j's distribution not conditioned on the choice at j-1) — e.g. DSpark's sequential correction head, consistency, CRF/semi-AR heads.

For each relevant paper give: title, arXiv id + month, venue if any, what exactly it does, and how close it is to the idea (identical / overlapping / adjacent). Also report whether the DFlash paper or code already supports tree verification, and whether vLLM (v0.16+ through 2026) supports tree attention for DFlash or any parallel drafter, and on ROCm. Be specific and concise; end with a 3-sentence verdict on what remains novel. Do not write files.

